Correct, the response is the proportion of time spent eating 7 different food items that were offered. I'm trying to determine preference with proportion of time spent "choosing" a food item as a proxy. If a mouse didn't eat at all (only a couple out of about 300) they are omitted.  So each mouse has a row for each food item, and all of those rows sum to 1 (per mouse).  There are very clear differences in the proportions for the foods, so I know there's something there. I've tried various model designs to account for the fact that each mouse sees each food. At the D-RUG open hours the other day someone sent me all of McElreath's stuff and I have started to go through it. I've got a date with Rosemary to try to figure it out, but we can keep chatting about it here if you guys are interested in chatting about what mice like to eat! 🐀🍻🍕

Thanks!
Katie

