> > > > > >
> > > > > > Typically, when lmer is having issues converging, either (1) the model is mis-specified (e.g., using a linear model with binary data, etc) or (2) the model is saturated (you have more predictors than information to estimate them). In this case, I would guess:
> > > > > >
> > > > > > PROP ~ FOOD + (1+FOOD|MOUSEID) + (1+FOOD|SITE)
> > > > > >
> > > > > > means you are trying to estimate a random intercept and slope of food for both individual mice (mouseid) and site, which can be difficult if you do not have multiple observations of both. You might be trying to stretch the data too far by estimating K parameters when K >> N.
